<%# THE POINTER AT /budget'S SUGGESTIONS (spec §8.1). Local: `presenter` (CategoryBudgetPresenter).

    ONE ARM NOW, WHERE IT SERVED TWO. §8.1 put this on the uncapped state and review added it to
    the account-pointed one, where it matters more; the uncapped state is deleted with the category
    cap (plan 3, task 3), so the arm that remains is the one this sentence was always most true of —
    nothing claims that category's spending, so it comes straight out of what is free to spend, and
    a rule of its own is its ONLY way out (computed-claims spec §3.3: every claim comes from a rule,
    and §5 closes the allocation that used to be the second door). Kept as a partial rather than
    inlined: it is still rendered from the block, and it reads the same presenter the card does.

    It renders ONLY when the engine currently proposes for this category
    (CategoryBudgetPresenter#suggestions), so it can never send a user to a panel with nothing in it
    for them.

    ** THE LINK IS `?open=<category>` NOW, AND NOT A FRAGMENT (two-shapes spec §4). ** It used to be
    `#suggestions-dated_bill` — the anchor of a run inside one page-wide panel — and there is no
    page-wide panel: every suggestion sits inside the category it is about. The category is what
    this card IS, so the pointer names it and the Budget page opens there with the proposals in
    view. One parameter, the same one the chevron on that page writes. %>
<div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-100" data-suggestion-pointer>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">
    Your spending here already looks like a rule — the Budget page is proposing
    <%= pluralize(presenter.suggestions.size, "rule") %> for this category.
  </p>
  <%# "it" OR "them", AGREEING WITH THE SENTENCE ABOVE IT. That line already pluralises through
      `pluralize` — "proposing 2 rules for this category" — and the link under it said "See it",
      which reads as a pointer at one of the two and leaves the other unaccounted for. %>
  <%= link_to budget_page_path(open: presenter.category.id),
              class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-brand hover:text-brand-dark" do %>
    <span>See <%= presenter.suggestions.size > 1 ? "them" : "it" %> on the Budget page</span>
    <%= heroicon "arrow-right", options: { class: "h-4 w-4" } %>
  <% end %>
</div>
